# Public projection consumer rules

- Consume only `professional-public-projection/v1` already present in this repo.
- Never read, clone, mount, query or fetch the private source during build,
  tests, preview or deploy.
- Reject unknown versions, unknown fields, prohibited private/internal material
  at any depth and missing/orphan/duplicate relations.
- Site and CV representations are independent; shared facts do not require
  identical copy.
- Make error behavior consistent and contextual. Do not hide relational failures
  behind a different undocumented interface.
- Generic helpers may accept test paths, but production entry points must use
  explicit repository-local files. Document the actual guarantee, not a stronger
  one.
- Tests must match their names: a recursive guarantee needs fixtures at several
  meaningful depths.
- Technical validity never authorizes publishing, deployment or repository
  visibility.
